// endpoint_merge_workspace.proto — MergeWorkspace. SIDEBAR section. A
// workspace LANDS ITS OWN BRANCH: rebased, gated and landed in its own
// worktree by its own session, its feed held and the merge bubble pinned until
// the merge ends, and the workspace closed once the branch lands. Success means
// ENQUEUED; everything after rides the streams.
//
// THE REQUEST NAMES NO TARGET. Where a workspace lands was fixed when it was
// created (agentrepl.v1.WorkspaceTopology): the primary branch, or the
// workspace that owns the branch it was cut from. The daemon reads it from the
// workspace's own record, so no request can land work anywhere else.
//
// WHO MAY ASK. The workspace itself, the user, or -- for a child -- the
// workspace that owns its branch. A child whose context was not forked from its
// owner never lands itself: its owner arbitrates its work and lands it
// (`owner_lands`).
